  "description": "Find the minimum number of operations to reduce x to zero by removing elements from either end. This is equivalent to finding the longest subarray whose sum equals (totalSum - x).",
  "target": 5,
  "pseudocode": "1. target = sum(nums) - x\n2. if target < 0 return -1\n3. left = 0, currentSum = 0, maxLen = -1\n4. for right = 0 to n-1:\n5.   currentSum += nums[right]\n6.   while currentSum > target:\n7.     currentSum -= nums[left++]\n8.   if currentSum == target:\n9.     maxLen = max(maxLen, right - left + 1)\n10. return n - maxLen if maxLen != -1 else -1",
